==English==
[[File:William Heysmann Overend Naval Captain on the Poop deck taffrail.jpg|right|thumb|''Naval Captain on the Poop Deck Taffrail'', by William Heysmann Overend]]

===Etymology===
From either {{m|en|tafferel}} or {{m|en|aft}} {{m|en|rail}}, by false alteration.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} The curved wooden top of the [[stern]] of a [[sailing]] [[man-of-war]] or [[East Indiaman]], usually [[carved]] or [[decorated]].
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[rail]] around the [[stern]] of a [[ship]].
#* '''1833''', {{w|Edgar Allan Poe}}, "MS. Found in a Bottle," [http://www.gutenberg.org/files/2147/2147-h/2147-h.htm#link2H_4_0013]
#*: One evening, leaning over the '''taffrail''', I observed a very singular, isolated cloud, to the N.W.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1851|author={{w|Herman Melville}}|title={{w|Moby-Dick}}|chapter=29|url=http://www.gutenberg.net.au/ebooks/z00015.html|passage={{...}} with heavy, lumber-like pace he was measuring the ship from '''taffrail''' to mainmast {{...}}}}
#:: See also citations under [[tafferel]].
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[deck]] area at the stern of a [[vessel]].

